WEBVTT

NOTE Sample material for trying Imprint. Cedar Hollow is a fictional city.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:11.000
<v Mayor Okafor>Next item is the warming center season report. Director Lindqvist, go ahead.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:26.000
<v Director Lindqvist>Thank you. The short version is that the center did what it was built to do. Eighty-seven nights open, and no one was turned away for lack of space.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:44.000
<v Director Lindqvist>The night that worried us most was January twenty-first. We had sixty-one guests in a hall set up for sixty. We opened the gym as overflow and it held.

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:19.000
<v Council Member Reyes>The east side question keeps coming up. People are walking across the Fifth Street bridge at two in the morning to get there. That is the part I can't get past.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:41.000
<v Director Lindqvist>That's why we're recommending a second site. We have a church on Ridge Avenue that has offered its fellowship hall. The estimate is about a hundred and forty-two thousand dollars for a full season.

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:22.000
<v Council Member Pham>What I want to see before budget is where the money comes from. The county grant was eighty thousand this year. Is that renewing?

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:39.000
<v Director Lindqvist>The county has told us informally they expect to renew at the same level. We won't have it in writing until April.

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:24.000
<v Mayor Okafor>Let's put the second site and the earlier opening date on the budget work session agenda for April 8. Thank you, Director.
